        "MetaKey": "use_cases",
        "Name": "use_cases",
        "ValueType": "array",
        "StringValue": null,
        "JsonValue": "[\"**Browse the substrate catalog.** Open `ExecutionSubstrates` and read the row for *PostgreSQL* — that is the production tool that generated this rulebook's SQL views; *Explain DAG* is the one rendering the rule-derivation visualizer in the portal.\", \"**Walk the demo gallery from the inside.** Each row in `RulebookDomains` is one of the sibling folders under `rulebook-examples/` — including a self-row for this rulebook in spirit, since it catalogs the same project it lives in.\", \"**Trace a flow end-to-end.** `CoreDataFlows` lists the five pipelines that move bits from Airtable through the rulebook into the substrates and back out as conformance reports; pick one and follow its Steps column.\", \"**Audit the dependency surface.** `Dependencies` is the honest list of what has to be installed for which substrates to run — Python is required, Go and .NET are optional, Airtable is one input spoke among several.\", \"**Reconcile the architecture against the code.** Compare a row in `OrchestrationComponents` to the actual file at that `FilePath`; if the rulebook drifts from the repo, this is the row that should be edited.\"]"
